@page "/scoreboard"
@using PullbackStrategyLab.Web.Shell
@model ScoreboardModel
@*
    The empty state, which is the whole page until 3.5. It names what will fill it and
    which checkpoint fills it, because an empty page that says so is honest and a page of
    invented rows is not.
*@
<h1>@Model.Item.Title</h1>
<p class="lede">@Model.Item.What.</p>

<div class="empty-state">
    <p><b>Nothing here yet.</b> This screen is filled at checkpoint @Model.Item.ArrivesAt.</p>
    <p>The shell, its navigation, the status band and the shared chart component are what
       checkpoint 1.8 built. Nothing on this page is stubbed with sample rows: a page of
       invented data reads as a working screen and is the one thing that cannot be told apart
       from the real one later.</p>
</div>
